      "role": "user",
      "content": "But aren't you kind of dodging the question? You said there's no absolute answer, but isn't it true that a country that sits by and watches a dictator rise when they have the power to stop it is actually failing its own moral duty to protect global human rights? If the goal is the preservation of liberty, then inaction is just as much a moral choice as intervention.",
